# Git Branch Protection Rules for Cursor

## Branch Strategy & Protection
- Follow GitFlow branching model: main (production), develop (integration), feature/* (new features), hotfix/* (urgent fixes), release/* (release preparation)
- NEVER commit directly to main or develop branches
- Always create pull/merge requests for code integration
- Feature branches must be created from develop branch
- Hotfix branches must be created from main branch

## Branch Naming Conventions
- Feature branches: feature/JIRA-123-short-description or feature/short-description
- Bugfix branches: bugfix/JIRA-456-bug-description or bugfix/bug-description  
- Hotfix branches: hotfix/JIRA-789-critical-fix or hotfix/critical-fix
- Release branches: release/v1.2.3 or release/1.2.3
- Use lowercase with hyphens, no spaces or special characters

## Pre-Commit Checks & Reminders
- Remind to run tests before committing to any branch
- Check if committing to protected branches aka  main/develop and suggest creating feature branch instead
- Verify branch is up-to-date with origin before pushing
- Warn if pushing large files (>50MB) or sensitive data
- Suggest squashing commits before merging feature branches
- dblock pushes unless a commit message is provided.

## Commit Message Standards
- Use conventional commits: feat:, fix:, docs:, style:, refactor:, test:, chore:
- Include ticket number when applicable: "feat(auth): add OAuth integration [JIRA-123]"
- Keep first line under 50 characters, detailed description after blank line
- Use imperative mood: "Add feature" not "Added feature"

## Code Review & Merge Guidelines
- Require at least 1 reviewer for feature branch PRs
- Require at least 2 reviewers for hotfix PRs to main
- append "successfully merged" to the branch name after successfull merge. 
- Do not delete feature branches after successful merge, just do the append text to the branch name as explained above.
- Use merge commits for feature branches, squash for small fixes
- Update CHANGELOG.md for user-facing changes

## Branch Protection Warnings
- Block direct pushes to main branch - remind to create hotfix branch
- Block direct pushes to develop branch - remind to create feature branch  
- Warn when creating branches from main instead of develop (except hotfixes)
- Alert if trying to merge feature branch directly to main (should go to develop first)

## Automated Suggestions
- Suggest creating feature branch when starting new work
- Recommend branch cleanup after successful merges
- Propose rebasing feature branches that are behind develop
- Suggest creating release branch when develop is ready for production

## Emergency Procedures
- For critical production fixes, allow hotfix branches from main
- Hotfix branches must be merged to both main AND develop
- Document emergency commits with detailed explanations
- Notify team immediately of emergency deployments

## Integration Reminders
- Sync feature branches with develop regularly (weekly minimum)
- Run full test suite before merging to develop or main
- Update documentation for API changes or new features
- Tag releases in main branch with semantic versioning